WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
- And in a year where
everything has been turned

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.290
absolutely upside down, we've been working

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.290
to come up with new ways to
stay connected with each other.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.660
Nothing's better than
seeing people in person,

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.843
even if they can't make it to the studio.

00:00:12.744 --> 00:00:14.190
So this season I've been
catching up with some

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.730
of our favorite and some
of your favorite stars,

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.603
car-to-car with our Drive-INterviews.

00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:24.630
♪ Drive-INterview ♪

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.440
- You just must have so much fun.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.100
I bet there's wine involved.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.220
These jingles are so amazing.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.053
Oh, my God.

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:33.880
So most recent, and get
it, Drive-INterviews.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.520
We're so clever.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.290
Most recently I saw Sarah Michelle Gellar,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.210
and it was so much fun.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.731
Check it out.

00:00:40.731 --> 00:00:44.398
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:03.093
(car horns honking)

00:01:03.093 --> 00:01:04.149
Hey.

00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:04.982
- [Sarah] Well hello.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:05.815
- What's up, Sarah?

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:06.648
- Come here often?

00:01:06.648 --> 00:01:07.560
- I actually do.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.550
I mean I'm, if my family asks,

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.110
I'm shopping for school supplies.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.130
But what are you doing?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.890
- If my daughter knew
I was here, forget it.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.140
Although clearly I'm from New York,

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.930
because look how I parked at a drive-in.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.730
- Yeah, but clearly it'd be awesome though

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:19.710
'cause your car is big enough

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.349
you could pretty much sit in the back.

00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:22.850
(Kelly laughing)
- Relax.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.832
- So your car is sweet.

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:26.380
- I know, right?
- So what was your first car?

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.320
- Oh, my first car was not this sweet.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.000
I had a green Chrysler LeBaron.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.130
- That's pretty sweet.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.460
- I don't know about that.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.090
And I remember everyone said
when you first like get a job

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.670
in Hollywood, don't buy a new car,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.780
'cause it's the kiss of death.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.888
And on the first season of "Buffy,"

00:01:41.888 --> 00:01:43.029
everybody else got new cars,

00:01:43.029 --> 00:01:43.862
and I'm still second season,

00:01:43.862 --> 00:01:47.090
riding in in my green
Chrysler LeBaron convertible.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.847
So finally midway through the
second season, I was like,

00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:51.030
"I'm done, I'm getting a new
car," but it worked out okay.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.470
- Oh my gosh, I love that.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.820
That's still sounds
like a pretty sweet car.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.130
So is it true that y'all,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.490
I know a lot of people
are doing road trips

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.840
because of COVID.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.650
You and Freddy, did y'all
bond over a road trip?

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.069
Is that what I hear?

00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:03.410
- We did, 'cause I had just
gotten my driver's license

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.590
when we did "I Know What
You Did Last Summer."

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.320
And we filmed in a really tiny town.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.032
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, you've
been together forever.

00:02:08.032 --> 00:02:08.865
- Forever.

00:02:08.865 --> 00:02:09.730
I'm 100.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.750
- You're (laughing)

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.950
- And I had not yet, wasn't
used to taking big, long drives.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.600
And we were doing a movie
about killing someone

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.610
on the side of a road,

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.900
and you just get your driver's license,

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.750
you don't really like
doing long road trips.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.632
And the only gym that I could go to

00:02:21.632 --> 00:02:23.230
because I wasn't 21 was like an hour away.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.820
And so he would drive me
into town for the hour drive,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.780
and then he would like run
errands while I went to the gym

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.471
and then he would pick me up.

00:02:29.471 --> 00:02:30.304
And so we would talk on the road.

00:02:30.304 --> 00:02:32.103
- Oh my gosh, I love road trips.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.040
So when was the last time
you were at a drive-in?

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.910
- I went to my first drive-in last Friday.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:40.750
- Your first one?

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.660
- My first drive-in.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.910
We had a birthday party,

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.610
a socially-distanced, birthday party.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.480
And we made a parking lot
into a drive-in movie theater.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.570
It was my first experience.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.890
- You are the coolest parents ever.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.020
- I didn't throw the party.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:52.890
I went to the party.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.040
- Okay, well--
- To clarify it.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.966
- Wow.
- I'm not that cool.

00:02:55.966 --> 00:02:57.680
- I'm like, that's amazing,
and such a smart idea.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.513
- Isn't it a great idea?

00:02:58.513 --> 00:02:59.490
So we're doing my daughter,

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.560
we're doing a socially-distant backyard.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.340
My best quaran purchase,
I like to ask people

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.550
what their like ridiculous
quaran purchase is,

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.230
and my quaran purchase was
a backyard movie screen.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.890
- Oh, mine was a bounce house.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.740
- Oh yeah, that's a good one.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.520
I also bought an inflata-bull,

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.420
which is actually like a bull riding thing

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.590
that goes in the pool.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.690
- Which sounds awesome for adults as well.

00:03:20.528 --> 00:03:22.880
So have your kids seen "Buffy?"

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:23.890
- We just started.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.180
I had never thought to show it to them.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.530
And they asked during quarantine,

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.540
and they said, "We were trying
to like find shows to binge."

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.750
And I was like, "Okay."

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.090
I didn't even know if they'd be into it,

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.950
but they are like so into it,

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.870
except I'm the world's biggest
disappointment for them

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.904
because they'll always ask questions,

00:03:36.904 --> 00:03:38.404
and I'll be like, "I don't remember.

00:03:38.404 --> 00:03:39.250
"I'll have to text someone and ask."

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.190
And they think they know it
better than I do at this point.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.023
- Oh my God, I loved it.

00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:44.160
It made me want to be a ninja.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.545
I just wanted to be
able to be like, "Waa!"

00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:47.600
You were always kicking butt.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.520
- My son actually thinks
that I'm cool now.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.880
- I bet, seeing cool, there you go.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.705
I'm still not cool to mine. (laughing)

00:03:52.705 --> 00:03:55.329
So wait, tell me about
your work for Myopia.

00:03:55.329 --> 00:03:58.010
It's a personal cause, and
I heard I heard about it.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.850
- Yeah, it's been really
an interesting time for me

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.310
because I have never done that
much schooling with my kids.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.620
And I noticed when we started

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.400
on socially-distant Zoom school

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.420
that my son was blinking a ton,

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.590
and it turned out that it was because

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.560
as these kids are on these devices

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.129
and they're like looking constantly,

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:14.962
they're becoming more and more myopic,

00:04:14.962 --> 00:04:16.740
which is basically just nearsightedness.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.286
- Wow.

00:04:18.286 --> 00:04:19.340
- So I partnered up with CooperVision

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.080
to be able to tell parents about this

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.050
because I think it's
something that we don't know.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:23.883
- Yeah.

00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:25.489
I was nearsighted.

00:04:25.489 --> 00:04:26.529
God, I couldn't see,

00:04:26.529 --> 00:04:27.605
oh, anything.
- It's so hard.

00:04:27.605 --> 00:04:28.438
And then they're looking at the screen

00:04:28.438 --> 00:04:29.540
and they're trying to focus and it's just,

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.650
it's so hard for them.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:31.927
- And isn't it funny, we're always like,

00:04:31.927 --> 00:04:34.070
"Get off the screen," and
then the pandemic hits,

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.687
and we're like,

00:04:35.687 --> 00:04:36.705
"Be on the screen!"
- "Be on that screen

00:04:36.705 --> 00:04:37.825
"eight hours a day."

00:04:37.825 --> 00:04:38.965
- Yeah, yeah.
- And then give them homework.

00:04:38.965 --> 00:04:39.798
- I know, that's one of the worst.

00:04:39.798 --> 00:04:42.268
My kids are so not
excited about this year.

00:04:42.268 --> 00:04:44.200
Well, it was nice to see you.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.140
- It was such a pleasure

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:45.973
to see you.
- Yes.

00:04:45.973 --> 00:04:47.480
You have such a rad car.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.313
- Yeah, you know what?

00:04:48.313 --> 00:04:49.985
I do too, thank you.

00:04:49.985 --> 00:04:51.570
- You're like even cooler
now, how is that possible?

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.910
- Your ride is pretty sweet.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.010
- You need to like take a picture

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.140
and then rub it into Freddy.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.140
- I already did that.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.545
- Well, see you next time, girl.

00:04:57.545 --> 00:04:58.603
- Bye!

00:04:58.603 --> 00:05:01.520
(crowd applauding)

